{
    "background_story": "Harlan was a brilliant physicist who spent his career studying the mysteries of magnetic fields. His obsession with toroids, doughnut-shaped coils that produce powerful magnetic fields, led to a groundbreaking discovery. Harlan's research revealed a novel way to harness the energy stored in toroids, paving the way for revolutionary advancements in power generation and storage. His work, though complex and often misunderstood, earned him recognition within the scientific community. Colleagues would often joke that Harlan's mind was shaped like a toroid, with ideas circulating in a continuous loop, always generating new insights. Harlan's dedication to his craft inspired a new generation of scientists, and his name became synonymous with innovation in the field of electromagnetism.",
